{
  "_schema": "nexus-rgb-reference-baselines/1",
  "_what": "Reduced, read-only reference values distilled from the SUPERSEDED pixels-only RGB campaigns (campaign 1 'pixels-only' and campaign 2 'shared encoder / pixel-aware meta'). These are the ONLY numbers the surviving state-vs-state+RGB campaign (campaign 3) quotes from that work: they appear as reference lines and comparison bars in figures 2, 4, 6, 7 and 8 and in the 'blind encoder' table of the analysis report.",
  "_source_tree": "results/rgb/ablation/<env>/<tag>/{pixel_ablation.json,training_curves.json} -- DELETED in the RGB refactor. The full artifacts (including PNGs, MP4s and the raw training curves) remain in git history at commit 8333c396fd21da13ef2caac538993749eddfb699 and earlier.",
  "_extraction": "Per run: every condition's value under the run's own metric key (reward_per_step_mean, or upright_fraction_mean for cartpole) was copied verbatim from pixel_ablation.json -> results; the intact condition additionally keeps its _std / _std_sample. pixel_sensitivity_last20 and train_return_last20 are the mean of the LAST 20 entries of training_curves.json -> curves.{pixel_sensitivity,episode_return}, the same reduction the plotting and analysis tools applied to the live curves, so the figures are numerically unchanged. No other field is derived.",
  "_budget": "Every run here: 250 updates x 128 envs x 64 steps = 2,048,000 env steps, matching the campaign-3 arms. Confirmed per run by the `updates` / `num_envs` fields below.",
  "_caveat": "All of these arms are RGB_PROPRIO: none (pixels-only) -- the actor got a camera INSTEAD of the state vector. Only cheetah's nesy_seed{0,1,2} differ from their campaign-3 counterpart in RGB_PROPRIO alone; cartpole/walker nesy_fixed_* also carry RGB_AUX_STATE_COEF 1.0 and META_DECISION_INTERVAL 4, and the nesy_shared* / *_metaz_* arms additionally enable the campaign-2 shared-encoder and pixel-aware-meta features. The tools that read this file already encode which contrasts are one-key; do not re-derive that from here.",
  "_not_captured": "results/rgb/ablation/hopper/nesy_seed0 was present in the deleted tree but referenced by no surviving tool, so it is not reproduced here. Likewise the deleted summary/ figures.",
  "_regenerated_by": "Nothing -- the inputs no longer exist in the working tree. To rebuild, check out 8333c396fd21da13ef2caac538993749eddfb699, restore results/rgb/ablation/ and re-run the extraction described in _extraction.",
